The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command in the instructions fails by design and the planner reads the file from disk. I briefly force-staged it by mistake and then unstaged it, so git is clean.

State of things. The harness found the build green at 70170ba2. The last 10 sessions landed 20 of 20 tasks with no reverts, and the last 4 evolve runs succeeded. I tried three things with the built binary and all behaved as designed: the GitHub provider refusal, the bad-key hint, and the unknown-flag refusal.

New bug, seen with the binary and filed as #1169. I made a temp repo with two edited files, neither staged.
• The REPL's startup banner says 1 staged, 1 modified. The truth is 0 staged, 2 modified.
• /git stage lists argo.toml instead of Cargo.toml. Picking it would try to stage a file that doesn't exist.
• Cause: the helpers git::run_git and run_git_in_dir call .trim() on git's output. That strips the leading space from the first line of git status --porcelain, and the parsers read that space as a status column.
• Source: Claude Code's changelog from today (2.1.321) fixed the same symptom. Checking its fixes against my own code turned up this one.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. #1168, filed by @yuanhao tonight. yoagent 0.27.7 is out and adds a preset for gemini-2.5-flash-lite, the last row of my hand-built GOOGLE_PUBLISHED_LIMITS table. He says the automatic upgrade to 0.27.7 will be rolled back until the table is deleted. His instructions: rework the guard tests rather than delete them, and the commit also fixes #1164.
2. #1169, the git status bug above. It's small and easy to check with a temp-repo test. The likely fix is trim_end() in the helper, but the helper has 103 callers, and they need checking for any that rely on the leading trim.
3. #1167. My copy of yoagent's list of "context too long" error phrases has drifted. It still contains the broad phrase "exceeds the maximum", which also matches Azure's peak-load rate-limit message, so yoyo compacts when it should retry. This is from reading the code; I haven't run it. yoagent has a public ProviderError::classify, so the copy can be tested against the dependency or replaced by it.

Size gate: two files are close to failing the module-size test. src/context.rs has no entry and is 15 lines from the limit; src/config.rs is 10 lines over its recorded size from the limit. Any task that adds to either has to update its entry in tests/module_size.rs, or the whole task gets reverted.

